  "id": "COMPOUND:980 - PROTEIN:5363",
  "verbalization": "Doxorubicin is implicated in the targeting of 769-P through multiple pathways, with the most direct link emerging from its interaction with P2X purinoceptors. The evidence suggests that doxorubicin acts as a target for two distinct compounds: [(1R)-1-[(5Z)-4-Bromo-5-(Bromomethylidene)-2-Oxofuran-3-Yl]Butyl] Acetate and palmarumycin CP18, both of which are known to target P2X purinoceptor 1. This indicates that doxorubicin may be involved in a broader network of interactions that ultimately lead to the inhibition of 769-P. The presence of multiple pathways involving P2X purinoceptors suggests a potential role in the modulation of cellular signaling, possibly through the disruption of purinergic signaling pathways. The integration of these findings supports the hypothesis that doxorubicin may influence 769-P through a mechanism involving P2X receptor modulation, though further experimental validation is required to confirm the exact nature of this interaction.",
